Sprint 13 — Audit Logs

IKM-13.1 — Global Admin Audit Trail

Goal

Provide immutable traceability for all state-changing administrative actions to ensure complete financial accountability.

Description

Implement an audit_logs table and an Interceptor or Service hook that captures the userId, the target entity, and the before/after state of the database row when critical changes occur.

Schema definition

id: uuid PK

admin_user_id: uuid FK -> users(id)

action_type: varchar (e.g., APPROVE_CONTRIBUTION, WAIVE_PENALTY)

entity_name: varchar

entity_id: uuid

old_state: jsonb

new_state: jsonb

created_at: timestamptz

API Endpoint

GET /api/v1/audit-logs

Authorization

@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard) with @Roles('ADMIN').

Implementation Constraints

The audit log creation must run in the same database transaction as the mutation itself. If the payment approval rolls back, the audit log must roll back.

This requires injecting the AuditService into the respective Repositories so that it can be appended via this.db.transaction().

Acceptance Criteria

 Migration creates the audit_logs table utilizing jsonb columns for state snapshots.

 Approving a payment records exactly one row mapping the admin's ID, the payment ID, and the status change {'status': 'PENDING'} -> {'status': 'APPROVED'}.

 GET /audit-logs successfully paginates the ledger for Admins.

 Audit insertions respect the unit-of-work/transaction boundary.
